+PDF and Office parsing runs in a disposable child process, using the same fixed
+worker protocol in source installations and the packaged runtime. Each worker
+has a 30-second limit, a 512 MiB process-memory limit, bounded output and a
+temporary home without inherited provider credentials or application settings.
+At most two extractions run concurrently per serving process. Failures, timeouts
+and malformed results refuse evidence; parsing never falls back into the server.
+Source bytes pass through stdin and are not saved to the temporary directory.
+This contains parser crashes and resource use; it is not an OS filesystem or
+network sandbox, and adds neither rendering nor OCR. The existing preview
+confirmation, source hashes and page/paragraph/cell citations remain required.
+
 Replacing or removing evidence clears the assessment and pending action approval.
