 These internally authored fixtures contain no customer or live vendor data. The PDF has three real pages, including a blank second page, to test source-grounded page locations. The text fixture deliberately contradicts its provenance and training-data claims. They demonstrate supported parsing and unresolved review; they are not compliance evidence or live acceptance.
 
 `northstar-policy.docx` and `northstar-policy.xlsx` are authored with python-docx and openpyxl by `make_office_fixtures.py`. They exercise Word body text and table paragraphs, Excel visible cells and a deliberately hidden contradictory row. The Word header is intentionally outside the supported scope. `northstar-scan.pdf` is a real raster-only PDF containing the same short synthetic provenance sentence; it requires the explicit human-transcription fallback, with no OCR claim. The generator's optional development libraries are not product or test-runtime dependencies.
+
+## Authored extraction corpus
+
+`document-corpus.json` pins the bytes, expected text, source locations, omissions and refusal outcomes of 14 selected cases. `evaluate_document_corpus.py` runs the current vendor extraction entry point and checks those expectations; it also checks citation source hashes and versions. Run from the repository root with the core package installed:
+
+```console
+python scripts/acceptance/fixtures/vendor-documents/evaluate_document_corpus.py --output authored-document-evaluation.json
+python -m pytest -q packages/maverick-core/tests/test_vendor_document_corpus.py
+```
+
+The baseline profile is `legacy_page_stream_and_office_body_cells`. It covers Word body/table paragraphs, omitted header/footer/hidden content, tracked-change refusal, Excel visible cells, hidden rows/columns/sheets, a deliberately stale cached formula result, and an uncached formula omission. Cached values are extracted as stored; formulas are not recalculated.
+
+The PDF cases include a supported three-page reference with a blank middle page and independently renderable authored digital, multicolumn, embedded-font/Unicode, rotated, image-only, low-quality and blank PDFs. The legacy parser refuses the latter fixtures; a passing baseline records those limitations rather than claiming successful extraction. A malformed PDF is separate from valid-but-unsupported layouts. Virtual oversized PDF and Office cases are assembled from small pinned fixtures and must be refused before a parser starts. Image-only and low-quality files have authored ground truth, but this baseline does not evaluate OCR, rendered review, reading order, representative accuracy or customer document acceptance. Any rendered/OCR backend needs its own explicit profile and results.
+
+`make_document_corpus.py` regenerates the 11 `corpus-*` binaries and manifest using optional development libraries: python-docx 1.2.0, openpyxl 3.1.5, ReportLab 4.4.9 and Pillow 12.3.0. It normalizes ZIP timestamps/order and uses ReportLab's invariant output and bundled Vera font (digest recorded in the manifest). These libraries are not required to evaluate the checked-in bytes. The fixture names, canaries and contents are authored test data, with no customer information or live vendor records.
